(vector (map (:adr/consequences "{:genapp_clj_third_consumer \"kotoba-lang/genapp-clj (ADR-2607011900) now has a third real consumer beyond mangaka/animeka, validating its generality sooner than the extraction ADR anticipated\", :smaller_operational_surface \"no new actor identity/DID/repo to track in the fleet's actor roster -- co-location avoided a fourth com-etzhayyim-* repo\", :coscientist_gap_is_explicit \"a stub render can never reach :commit without a human -- the missing tournament doesn't weaken the safety invariant, every render just needs a human look until a gateway is actually configured\", :placement_precedent_is_per_work \"tsumugu's separate-actor-repo placement is not treated as a universal rule going forward -- confirmed by this ADR diverging from it on explicit direction\"}"), (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "SHIRO & PICO's publish actor (shiropico.*: cacao/kotoba identity, store, render, advisor, policy, phase, operation) lives at orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico/clj/, NOT as a separate orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-* actor repo -- diverges from com-etzhayyim-tsumugu's placement precedent by explicit session direction, per-work call not a universal rule" "shiropico.advisor does one real genapp.comfy render and derives confidence from :source (\"gateway\"=1.0 vs \"stub\"=0.3, below the 0.4 policy floor) -- it does NOT port tsumugu.coscientist's multi-strategy bonus-tag tournament, because animeka's cut domain has no equivalent multi-candidate free-text specification step to tournament over; inventing one would not be grounded" "shiropico.render builds directly on kotoba-lang/genapp-clj (own ShiropicoKSampler config), NOT on ai-gftd-animeka itself -- confirmed via grep that animeka's own generation graphs don't yet call animeka.comfy/animeka.llm at all, so wrapping animeka's registry would add an app-on-app dependency without adding real behavior" "the actor's mechanical skeleton (cacao/kotoba/store/policy/phase/operation) is a faithful structural port of com-etzhayyim-tsumugu, with only domain-shape renames (chapter/panel -> episode/cut) -- the StateGraph topology, confidence-floor/high-stakes governor shape, and phase-gate semantics are unchanged")), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/topic "shiropico-publish-actor"), (:adr/related (vector "CLAUDE.md" "90-docs/adr/2607011500-ghosthacker-sip-atproto-actor.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607011816-ghosthacker-shiropico-standalone-repo.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607011900-genapp-clj-mangaka-animeka-commons.edn" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-tsumugu" "orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico PR #2 (feat/shiropico-publish-actor)")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607012000-shiropico-publish-actor"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-01"), (:adr/body "# ADR 2607012000: SHIRO & PICO cut publish actor (shiropico.*, co-located in ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico)\n\n## Status\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nFollowing the \"should this be an actor?\" question from the earlier\nmangaka/animeka investigation: `com-etzhayyim-tsumugu` already proves this\npattern works for manga (Spirit in Physics) — self-sovereign CACAO identity,\ncontainment node (proposal-only), independent PolicyGovernor, StateGraph\n`intake → advise → govern → decide → commit|hold|approval`, append-only\nledger. Its own repo is fully materialized (23 tests / 62 assertions,\nlive-tested against kotobase.net). Given ADR-2607011816 established that\n`ai-gftd-animeka`, not `ai-gftd-mangaka`, is SHIRO & PICO's structurally\ncorrect production engine (`work → episode → scene → cut` domain, matching\nan anime not a manga), the natural next actor is one for SHIRO & PICO built\non animeka's domain shape.\n\nTwo design questions needed resolving before writing code:\n\n1. **Where does the actor's coscientist quality loop come from?** tsumugu's\n   coscientist runs a multi-strategy bonus-tag tournament over manga\n   storyboard panel text fields (`:colorNote`/`:narration`/`:description`).\n   Investigating animeka's actual domain (`clj/src/animeka/domain.cljc`)\n   found no equivalent — a cut's render spec is a direct prompt/negative/\n   seed, not derived from several competing free-text sources to tournament\n   over. Inventing a fictional multi-candidate strategy space to mirror\n   tsumugu's shape would not be grounded in anything real about how cuts\n   are actually specified.\n2. **Where does the code live — a new `com-etzhayyim-*` actor repo (matching\n   tsumugu's precedent), or inside `ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico`?** Initial\n   work started building `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-michibiki` (mirroring\n   tsumugu's placement exactly: `repos.edn`'s own taxonomy assigns\n   `etzhayyim` the role \"agent-centric — com-etzhayyim-* organism actors\").\n   Explicit direction during this session redirected it: the actor should\n   live inside `ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico` (the content repo,\n   ADR-2607011816), not as a separate actor-identity repo.\n\n## Decision\n\n### Domain-grounded advisor, not a fabricated tournament\n\n`shiropico.advisor` does one real render via `shiropico.render`\n(`genapp.comfy`-backed) and derives its proposal's confidence from what\n*actually happened*: `1.0` if the render reached a configured ComfyUI\ngateway (`:source \"gateway\"`), a fixed `0.3` if it degraded to the offline\nplaceholder (`:source \"stub\"`) — below the PolicyGovernor's `0.4` confidence\nfloor, so a stub render always escalates for human review, never silently\nauto-commits. This is a smaller, more honest containment node than\ntsumugu's coscientist: no invented candidate-strategy vocabulary, just a\nreal render outcome as the trust signal. `tsumugu.coscientist`'s\ngenerate/review/rank/evolve/meta-review loop shape (itself ported from\n`com-etzhayyim-ibuki`) remains available to port later if/when SHIRO & PICO\ngrows an equivalent multi-candidate specification step worth tournamenting\nover — nothing here forecloses that.\n\n### Co-located with content, not a separate actor repo\n\n`shiropico.*` lives at `orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico/clj/`\n(a sibling `clj/` subdirectory next to the content data, mirroring\n`ai-gftd-mangaka`'s and `ai-gftd-animeka`'s own `clj/` + data layout), not\nas a new `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-shiropico`-style repo. This means:\n\n- No new GitHub repo, no new manifest registration — the actor rides on\n  `ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico`'s existing west.yml entry; only its pin\n  needed advancing.\n- The publish actor's lifecycle (episode additions, cut backlog) stays\n  coupled to the content it publishes, one repo, one issue tracker.\n- Diverges from `tsumugu`'s placement (a separate `com-etzhayyim-*` actor\n  repo publishing content that itself lives in a different org/repo,\n  `org-spirit-in-physics-comics`) — that split precedent is not treated as\n  universal; each work's actor placement is a per-work call.\n\n### Ported mechanically from tsumugu, adapted only where the domain differs\n\n| tsumugu (manga: chapter → panel) | shiropico (anime: episode → cut) | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tsumugu.cacao` | `shiropico.cacao` | namespace rename + `default-db-name` \"manga\"→\"anime\" only — the crypto/SIWE/CBOR logic is already 100% domain-agnostic |\n| `tsumugu.kotoba` | `shiropico.kotoba` | namespace rename only |\n| `tsumugu.store` (chapter/panel) | `shiropico.store` (episode/cut) | schema fields renamed to match animeka's own domain granularity |\n| `tsumugu.render` (wraps `kami.mangaka.render`) | `shiropico.render` (wraps `genapp.comfy` directly) | **not** a dependency on `ai-gftd-animeka` — a third independent `genapp-clj` consumer, own `ShiropicoKSampler` config |\n| `tsumugu.mangallm` + `tsumugu.coscientist` | `shiropico.advisor` | simplified to a single grounded render + source-derived confidence (see above) — no coscientist port |\n| `tsumugu.policy` | `shiropico.policy` | same hard/soft two-check shape; hard = no such cut, soft = stub render OR `:high-stakes?` cut (SHIRO & PICO's henshin-bank transformation sequence, shared across every episode per `SERIES-BIBLE.md`, is the concrete example) |\n| `tsumugu.phase` | `shiropico.phase` | verbatim shape, `:panel/compose`→`:cut/render` op |\n| `tsumugu.operation` | `shiropico.operation` | verbatim StateGraph topology, field renames only (panel-id→cut-id, chapter-id→episode-id) |\n\n## Consequences\n\n- 19 tests / 49 assertions green (`cacao_test`, `store_test`,\n  `operation_test` — MemStore ≡ DatomicStore parity, phase 0/1/2 gating,\n  approval/rejection, missing-cut/episode holds, high-stakes escalation).\n  Offline-only (no live kotobase.net round-trip attempted) — matches\n  tsumugu's own current state (still blocked on a server-side deploy per\n  the investigation that preceded this ADR).\n- `genapp-clj` (ADR-2607011900) now has a third real consumer beyond\n  mangaka/animeka, validating its generality sooner than expected.\n- No new actor identity/DID/repo to track in the fleet's actor roster —\n  smaller operational surface than a fourth `com-etzhayyim-*` repo would\n  have been.\n- The coscientist-quality gap is explicit, not silently skipped: a stub\n  render can never reach `:commit` without a human, so the missing\n  tournament doesn't weaken the safety invariant, it just means every\n  render needs a human look until a gateway is actually configured.\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n1. **Full tsumugu-shape port, including a fabricated multi-strategy\n   coscientist tournament for cuts**: rejected — there is no real\n   multi-candidate specification step in animeka's cut domain to\n   tournament over; inventing one would be unverified, unjustified domain\n   modeling under time pressure, not a grounded design.\n2. **New `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-michibiki` actor repo** (tsumugu's\n   exact placement precedent): built first, then redirected per explicit\n   session direction to co-locate with `ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico`\n   instead. Superseded before merge — no trace left in west.yml/repos.edn.\n3. **Wrap `ai-gftd-animeka`'s own registry handlers as the containment\n   node** (reusing animeka's `generate-*` graphs instead of calling\n   `genapp.comfy` directly): investigated and rejected — animeka's own\n   generation graphs are not yet wired to call `animeka.comfy`/`animeka.llm`\n   at all (confirmed via grep: zero external callers of either namespace),\n   so routing through them would not produce any more real behavior than\n   calling `genapp.comfy` directly, while adding an app-on-app dependency\n   an actor shouldn't have.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607011500 (Spirit in Physics as a self-sovereign atproto actor —\n  the pattern this ADR reuses)\n- ADR-2607011816 (ghosthacker-shiropico standalone repo — corrected\n  animeka, not mangaka, as SHIRO & PICO's engine)\n- ADR-2607011900 (genapp-clj commons extraction — `shiropico.render`'s\n  third consumer)\n- `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-tsumugu` (the ported precedent)\n- `orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico` PR #2"), (:adr/decision "{:advisor_design {:approach \"shiropico.advisor calls shiropico.render (genapp.comfy-backed) once per request and derives :confidence from the render result's :source field: 1.0 for \\\"gateway\\\" (real render reached a configured ComfyUI endpoint), 0.3 for \\\"stub\\\" (offline placeholder) -- 0.3 is fixed below policy's 0.4 confidence-floor so stub renders always escalate, never silently auto-commit\", :not_ported \"tsumugu.coscientist's generate/review/rank/evolve/meta-review multi-strategy tournament -- no equivalent multi-candidate specification step exists in animeka's cut domain to tournament over; deferred, not foreclosed, if/when SHIRO & PICO grows one\"}, :placement {:location \"orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico/clj/ (sibling clj/ subdir next to the content data, mirroring ai-gftd-mangaka's and ai-gftd-animeka's own clj/+data layout)\", :not \"a new orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-shiropico-style actor repo (tsumugu's own placement precedent)\", :consequence \"no new GitHub repo, no new manifest registration -- rides on ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico's existing west.yml entry, only its pin needed advancing (09cbea7 -> 6e61ea6)\"}, :porting_map {:michibiki_cacao->shiropico_cacao \"namespace rename + default-db-name \\\"manga\\\"->\\\"anime\\\" only -- crypto/SIWE/CBOR logic already 100% domain-agnostic\", :kotoba \"namespace rename only\", :store \"chapter/panel schema fields renamed to episode/cut, matching animeka's own domain granularity\", :render \"wraps genapp.comfy directly (own ShiropicoKSampler config), NOT ai-gftd-animeka -- third independent genapp-clj consumer\", :mangallm+coscientist->advisor \"collapsed into one simpler render+confidence node, per :advisor_design above\", :policy \"same hard/soft two-check shape; hard=no-such-cut, soft=stub-render-OR-:high-stakes?-cut (henshin-bank transformation sequence per SERIES-BIBLE.md is the concrete high-stakes example)\", :phase \"verbatim shape, :panel/compose -> :cut/render op\", :operation \"verbatim StateGraph topology (intake->advise->govern->decide->commit|hold|request-approval, interrupt-before #{:request-approval}), field renames only\"}, :verification \"19 tests / 49 assertions green (cacao_test, store_test, operation_test: MemStore==DatomicStore parity, phase 0/1/2 gating, approval/rejection, missing-cut/episode holds, high-stakes escalation). Offline only, no live kotobase.net round-trip -- matches tsumugu's own current state (still blocked on a server-side deploy).\"}"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/problem "{:source \"user request 2026-07-01: continuation of 'proceed with 1, 2, 3' -- task 3 was 'should this be an actor?', answered yes in the prior exploratory turn citing com-etzhayyim-tsumugu as the proven working precedent (23 tests/62 assertions, live-tested against kotobase.net)\", :investigated [\"com-etzhayyim-tsumugu is fully materialized locally (not just an ADR) -- read all 9 source files (cacao.clj 229 lines, kotoba.clj 73, store.cljc 111, operation.cljc 156, policy.cljc 58, phase.cljc 44, mangallm.cljc 97, coscientist.cljc 209) plus its 4 test files, to port accurately rather than reconstruct from description\" \"tsumugu.coscientist's injection point (catalog + review's cond-> gate list, per the earlier research agent's ibuki-to-tsumugu port analysis) requires a multi-candidate free-text extraction domain (colorNote/narration/description panel fields) that animeka's cut schema (clj/src/animeka/domain.cljc: work->episode->scene->cut, :cut/stage-status) has no equivalent of -- a cut's render spec is a direct prompt, not synthesized from competing text sources\" \"grep confirmed animeka's own graphs/generation.cljc never calls animeka.comfy or animeka.llm (zero external callers of either namespace outside their own defining files) -- animeka's Phase-2 generation graphs are still stubs, so wrapping animeka's registry as containment would not produce any more real behavior than calling genapp.comfy directly\" \"tsumugu.operation_test.clj's actual assertions (langgraph.graph/run* with :thread-id/:resume?, {:status :interrupted}, get-in res [:state :disposition]) gave the exact langgraph-clj API surface needed to port the test suite correctly, not just the source\"], :risk \"a mid-build course correction happened: work started under orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-michibiki (mirroring tsumugu's separate-actor-repo placement) before explicit session direction redirected it into ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico/clj/ -- handled by moving the already-written .clj/.cljc files (sed-renaming the michibiki.* namespace to shiropico.* and MICHIBIKI_* env vars to SHIROPICO_*), verifying no residual 'michibiki' references, and deleting the abandoned directory before it was ever committed or pushed, so no trace landed in git history or the manifest\"}"), (:adr/alternatives "[{:option \"full tsumugu-shape port including a fabricated multi-strategy coscientist tournament for cuts\", :rejected_because \"no real multi-candidate specification step exists in animeka's cut domain to tournament over; inventing one would be unverified, unjustified domain modeling under time pressure\"} {:option \"new orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-michibiki actor repo (tsumugu's exact placement precedent)\", :rejected_because \"built first, then explicitly redirected mid-session to co-locate with ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico instead; superseded before merge, no trace in west.yml/repos.edn\"} {:option \"wrap ai-gftd-animeka's own registry handlers as the containment node instead of calling genapp.comfy directly\", :rejected_because \"animeka's own generation graphs are not yet wired to call animeka.comfy/animeka.llm at all (zero external callers confirmed via grep) -- routing through them would add an app-on-app dependency without producing any more real behavior than calling genapp.comfy directly\"}]"), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607012000: SHIRO & PICO cut publish actor (shiropico.*, co-located in ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico)"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))